                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 10.13: Bottle garden"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.29,
            0.368,
            0.883,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "plant. If the plant is growing well that means the plant is maintaining the exchange of gases, that is, carbon dioxide produced in the process of respiration of the plant is utilised for performing photosynthesis, and oxygen generated in photosynthesis is utilised in respiration by the plant inside the bottle."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.481,
            0.882,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How are plant processes like photosynthesis, respiration, and water and food transportation crucial for crop production?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.52,
            0.883,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Visit a greenhouse, if there is one near your place. Observe how people grow plants in a green house. Find out how they regulate the amount of light, water, and carbon dioxide used to grow plants."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.628,
            0.363,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "KNOW A SCIENTIST"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.652,
            0.767,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Kamala Sohonie (1911–1998) was a woman scientist of India. She received a Ph.D. degree for her remarkable contribution in the area of"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.69,
            0.328,
            0.836
          ],
